      "text": "To solve for the integer \\( n \\) such that \\( 0 \\leq n \\leq 7 \\) and \\( n \\equiv -3737 \\pmod{8} \\), we need to find the remainder when \\(-3737\\) is divided by \\(8\\). This can be done by first finding the remainder when \\(3737\\) is divided by \\(8\\), and then using that to find the remainder of \\(-3737\\) when divided by \\(8\\).\n\nFirst, we perform the division of \\(3737\\) by \\(8\\):\n\\[ 3737 \\div 8 = 467 \\text{ remainder } 1. \\]\nThis can be written as:\n\\[ 3737 = 8 \\cdot 467 + 1. \\]\nSo, the remainder when \\(3737\\) is divided by \\(8\\) is \\(1\\). Therefore,\n\\[ 3737 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{8}. \\]\n\nNext, we need to find the remainder when \\(-3737\\) is divided by \\(8\\). Using the property of congruences that \\(-a \\equiv -1 \\cdot a \\pmod{8}\\), we have:\n\\[ -3737 \\equiv -1 \\cdot 3737 \\pmod{8}. \\]\nSince \\(3737 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{8}\\), we get:\n\\[ -3737 \\equiv -1 \\pmod{8}. \\]\nTo express \\(-1\\) as a positive remainder, we add \\(8\\) to \\(-1\\):\n\\[ -1 + 8 = 7. \\]\nTherefore,\n\\[ -3737 \\equiv 7 \\pmod{8}. \\]\n\nThus, the integer \\( n \\) is \\(\\boxed{7}\\).",
