      "text": "To find the integer \\( n \\) such that \\( 0 \\le n \\le 7 \\) and \\( n \\equiv -3737 \\pmod{8} \\), we need to determine the remainder when \\( -3737 \\) is divided by \\( 8 \\). This is equivalent to finding \\( -3737 \\mod 8 \\).\n\nFirst, we find the remainder when \\( 3737 \\) is divided by \\( 8 \\). We do this by performing the division:\n\n\\[ 3737 \\div 8 = 467 \\text{ remainder } 1. \\]\n\nSo, we can write:\n\n\\[ 3737 = 8 \\cdot 467 + 1. \\]\n\nThis means that:\n\n\\[ 3737 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{8}. \\]\n\nNow, we need to find the remainder when \\( -3737 \\) is divided by \\( 8 \\). Since \\( -3737 \\equiv -1 \\pmod{8} \\), we need to express \\( -1 \\) in terms of a positive remainder between \\( 0 \\) and \\( 7 \\):\n\n\\[ -1 \\equiv 7 - 1 \\equiv 6 \\pmod{8}. \\]\n\nTherefore, the remainder when \\( -3737 \\) is divided by \\( 8 \\) is \\( 6 \\), so:\n\n\\[ n \\equiv -3737 \\pmod{8} \\implies n \\equiv 6 \\pmod{8}. \\]\n\nThus, the value of \\( n \\) is \\(\\boxed{6}\\).",
