      "text": "Given the requirement to find the integer $n$ such that $0 \\leq n \\leq 7$ and \\[\nn \\equiv -3737 \\pmod{8},\n\\] we start by determining the value of $-3737 \\mod 8$.\n\nFirst, we find the remainder when 3737 is divided by 8. We perform the division:\n\n\\[\n3737 \\div 8 = 467 \\text{ remainder } 1.\n\\]\n\nThis can be expressed as:\n\n\\[\n3737 = 8 \\cdot 467 + 1,\n\\]\n\nThus,\n\n\\[\n3737 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{8}.\n\\]\n\nTherefore,\n\n\\[\n-3737 \\equiv -1 \\pmod{8}.\n\\]\n\nNext, we convert $-1$ to a positive equivalent modulo 8. Since $-1$ is equivalent to $7$ modulo 8 (because $-1 + 8 = 7$):\n\n\\[\n-1 \\equiv 7 \\pmod{8}.\n\\]\n\nThus, the integer $n$ that satisfies the given condition is\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{7}.\n\\]",
